<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 7 September, from 1159 to 1940.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1159">1159 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">867 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A divided election makes Alexander III pope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the death of Adrian IV, a majority of the cardinals elected Cardinal Rolando of Siena as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-iii">Pope Alexander III</a>, but a minority chose Ottaviano de Monticelli as Victor IV, beginning a schism that lasted until 1178.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-iii">Pope Alexander III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1191">1191 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">835 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard the Lionheart defeats Saladin at Arsuf</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marching down the coast, Richard's army withstood harassing attacks before a crusader charge broke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s forces at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a>. The victory let the crusaders take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1228">1228 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">798 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick II lands at Acre on the Sixth Crusade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> and was warmly received by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Templars</a>, Hospitallers and clergy, but, being excommunicated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ix">Pope Gregory IX</a>, was denied the kiss of peace. Without a major battle, he negotiated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>'s return to Christian rule in 1229.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixth-crusade">Sixth Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1303">1303 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">723 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French troops seize Pope Boniface VIII at Anagni</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-boniface-viii">Pope Boniface VIII</a> excommunicated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-france">Philip IV of France</a>, the king's troops, led by his councillor Guillaume de Nogaret, attacked the pope's residence at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anagni">Anagni</a> and captured him. Boniface was held for three days and died a month later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-boniface-viii">Pope Boniface VIII</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-france">Philip IV of France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1533">1533 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">493 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The future Elizabeth I is born at Greenwich</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Anne Boleyn gave birth to a daughter, Elizabeth, a disappointment to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>, who wanted a son. As queen for 44 years she defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Armada</a> and presided over a golden age of English culture.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The submarine Turtle makes the first submarine attack</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sergeant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezra">Ezra</a> Lee steered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Bushnell's one-man submarine Turtle towards HMS Eagle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Harbor. He failed to attach the charge to the hull, but it was the first submarine attack in war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1812">1812 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon and Kutuzov fight the Battle of Borodino</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 70,000 men fell at Borodino, the bloodiest single day of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>. The Russians withdrew, and a week later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> entered an abandoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> that was soon ablaze.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Blitz begins with a massive raid on London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luftwaffe">Luftwaffe</a> switched to bombing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, starting 57 consecutive nights of raids. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-blitz">The Blitz</a> killed some 43,000 civilians by May 1941 but failed to break British morale.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
